        "note": "Etienne Marion, A Formalization of the Ionescu-Tulcea Theorem in Mathlib. DenseTime/Trajectory.lean uses Mathlib's Kernel.traj to construct the countable dense-time trajectory as a kernel in the starting point.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "arxiv:2511.20118v1",
        "note": "Rémy Degenne, David Ledvinka, Etienne Marion, and Peter Pfaffelhuber, Formalization of Brownian motion in Lean. Related work on process construction and Kolmogorov-Chentsov continuity. This library uses Mathlib's IsKolmogorovProcess predicate and supplies its own dyadic continuity proof for general semigroup trajectories. The selected theorem concerns general conservative Feller semigroups, not just Gaussian increments. No priority claim is made for this submission.",
